{"availability":"available","full":"imperial-nsb/jbubble","name":"jbubble","description":"🫧 Differentiable microbubble dynamics in JAX.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":16,"forks":2,"created":"2025-12-03T14:20:49Z","updated":"2026-10-07T01:37:51Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://imperial-nsb.github.io/jbubble/","topics":[],"demo":"https://imperial-nsb.github.io/jbubble/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:37.881Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:37.881Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:37.881Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:37.881Z","stars":16,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A free bubble 2 µm in radius, drawn to scale, under a six-cycle, 1 MHz, 120 kPa tone burst. See example 01: first simulation.","jax.grad and optax climb a GridSweep response map to the resonance peak. See example 09: gradients and optimisation.","A neural network learns a lipid shell's surface tension law from radius curves, against the true Marmottant law. See example 11: learn a shell law."],"features":["Compiled simulations. jax.jit compiles a model once. Later calls with new parameter values reuse the compiled solver.","Batched sweeps. jax.vmap simulates multiple bubble-pulse configurations in one call, and GridSweep provides a convenient utility for parameter sweeps.","Gradients and fitting. jax.grad gives the derivative of any output with respect to any model parameter. fitparameters is a utility that fits parameters to measured radius curves or emission signals with optax, with…","Composable physics. Multiple equations of motion are provided (Rayleigh-Plesset, Keller-Miksis, ...), which are composed with gas, shell, and medium laws, for a wide range of easily configurable modelling options.","Neural components. Replace a physical law, such as the shell's surface tension, with a NeuralProperty, or the drive with a NeuralPulse, and train it from data or some desired criteria using gradients."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imperial-nsb/jbubble/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1cf61c63bbce0e7a722a565aa0a312d32a5853db81f80b1f9705db325cdd729e","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:38.177Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:38.177Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A free bubble 2 µm in radius, drawn to scale, under a six-cycle, 1 MHz, 120 kPa tone burst. See example 01: first simulation.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imperial-nsb/jbubble/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"1cf61c63bbce0e7a722a565aa0a312d32a5853db81f80b1f9705db325cdd729e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imperial-nsb/jbubble/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:38.177Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T01:37:51Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imperial-nsb/jbubble/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:38.178Z","hash":"1cf61c63bbce0e7a722a565aa0a312d32a5853db81f80b1f9705db325cdd729e","originalBytes":9400,"storedBytes":9400,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["jbubble","see","bubble","install","pressure","pulse","radius","run","shell","simulation","eom","first","guide","import","jax","jax.grad","lipid","model","peak","compiled","example","examples","expansion","jax.vmap","law","open","parameter","parameters","pip","print","python","repository","add","any","bash","batched","biopsy","bubbles","build","call","cite","colab","contributing","curves","data","details","development","differentiable","documentation","driven","dynamics","e-6","each","eom.r0","freq","gas","gridsweep","ieee","installation","installs","international","ius","jax.","jax.jit","kpa","later","license","medium","mhz","microbubble","modelling","multiple","neural","noninvasive","one","optax","presented","pressures","project","quickstart","release","simulates","such","surface","surgery","sweeps.","symposium","tension","tone","ultrasonics","under","utility","acce